course: dictionary
lesson: 354
title: Words that mislead: antbird
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: An antbird is a small bird that lives in the tropical forests of Central and South America. Its name has the word ant in it, but the name does not tell the whole story. Context helps you check what a word really means.
explain: The sentence says: «Army ants raid in a moving carpet of hundreds of thousands, and antbirds follow to catch the insects fleeing in front, not to eat the ants.» The words «not to eat the ants» are a clue. The writer is correcting the idea you might get from the name.
explain: Look at the other clue words: follow, catch, fleeing. Army ants move in a huge group and scare insects into running away. Antbirds follow the ants and catch those insects as they run. So an antbird is a bird that follows ants to catch insects, and it mostly eats insects, not ants.
fact: An antbird is a small bird of the tropical forests of Central and South America.
fact: Some antbirds follow army ants to catch the insects that flee from them.
fact: Antbirds mostly eat insects, not ants.
fact: Army ants raid in a moving carpet of hundreds of thousands of ants.
fact: A name can give you a clue, but the sentences around a word show you what it really means.
exercise: What do antbirds mostly eat? | Seeds | Ants | Fish | *Insects
exercise: Where do antbirds live? | Deep oceans | *Tropical forests of Central and South America | Cold mountains of Canada | Deserts of Africa
exercise: The name antbird might make you think it eats ants. What does the sentence «not to eat the ants» tell you? | *The name misleads: antbirds catch insects fleeing from the ants | Antbirds only eat seeds | Army ants are a kind of bird | Antbirds eat the ants
test: In «antbirds follow to catch the insects fleeing in front», what are the insects doing? | *Running away from the ants | Eating the antbirds | Sleeping in the nest | Building a nest
test: Why do antbirds follow army ants? | *To catch the insects that flee from the ants | To find flowers to sleep in | To eat the army ants | To keep warm
exam: Which best describes an antbird? | A large bird that lives in the Arctic | *A small tropical forest bird that catches insects fleeing from army ants | A fish that swims alongside army ants | An insect that eats ants
